@constructive_roll_2026
title: Constructive roll call
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const relationRecruit =
    Math.round(
        Math.max(0, 38 - (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0)) / 4
    ) +
    Math.round(
        Math.max(0, 35 - (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0)) / 5
    );
const coalitionDefections = Math.round(
    Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 35
    ) / 5
);
const roll = Math.floor(
    (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 9
) - 4;
Q.constructive_relation_recruits = relationRecruit;
Q.constructive_coalition_defections = coalitionDefections;
Q.constructive_roll_variance = roll;
Q.constructive_yes = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        460,
        Math.round(Number(Q.constructive_base) || 0) +
            relationRecruit +
            coalitionDefections +
            roll
    )
);
Q.constructive_passed = Q.constructive_yes >= 231 ? 1 : 0;
Q.confidence_yes = Q.constructive_yes;
Q.confidence_abstain = Math.min(
    460 - Q.confidence_yes,
    20,
    4 + coalitionDefections
);
Q.confidence_no = Math.max(
    0,
    460 - Q.confidence_yes - Q.confidence_abstain
);
Q.confidence_candidate = Q.constructive_candidate;
Q.confidence_mode = "Constructive no confidence";
Q.confidence_present = 460;
Q.confidence_threshold = 231;
if (Q.constructive_passed) {
    Q.prime_minister = Q.constructive_candidate;
    Q.government_name = Q.constructive_candidate + " replacement cabinet";
    Q.government_party = "pis";
    Q.government_owner = "PiS and its governing partners";
    Q.left_in_government = 0;
    Q.left_cabinet_committed = 0;
    Q.left_cabinet_model = "Opposition";
    Q.ministries_finalized = 1;
    Q.ministry_allocation_mode = "settled";
    Q.ministry_return_mode = "event_queue";
    Q.budget = 0;
    Q.budget_authority =
        "Opposition — no state spending authority";
    Q.position = "Parliamentary opposition";
    Q.coalition_status = "Constructive replacement majority";
    Q.coalition_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0);
    Q.government_support_seats = Q.constructive_yes;
    Q.government_has_confidence = 1;
    Q.caretaker_government = 0;
    Q.formation_in_progress = 0;
    Q.formation_complete = 1;
    Q.coalition_broken = 0;
    Q.snap_election_requested = 0;
    if ((Number(Q.constructive_left_defections) || 0) > 0) {
        const durableLeftDefections = Math.min(
            Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)),
            Math.max(
                0,
                Math.round(
                    Number(Q.constructive_left_defections) || 0
                )
            )
        );
        Q.left_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) - durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.left_committed_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0) -
                durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.left_family_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.left_family_seats) || 0) -
                durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.coalition_democratic_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.coalition_democratic_seats) || 0) -
                durableLeftDefections
        );
        Q.other_seats =
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.other_seats) || 0) +
            durableLeftDefections;
    }
    const replacementCabinet = {
        labor: ["PiS", "Dorota Bojemska"],
        equality: ["PiS", "PiS equality nominee"],
        housing: ["PiS", "PiS housing nominee"],
        health: ["PiS", "Ewa Krajewska"],
        digital: ["PiS", "PiS digital-affairs nominee"],
        science: ["PiS", "Krzysztof Szczucki"],
        interior: ["PiS", "Paweł Szefernaker"],
        finance: ["PiS", "Andrzej Kosztowniak"],
        economy: ["PiS", "Marlena Maląg"],
        justice: ["PiS", "Marcin Warchoł"],
        foreign: ["PiS", "Szymon Szynkowski vel Sęk"],
        agriculture: ["PiS", "Anna Gembicka"],
        defence: ["PiS", "Mariusz Błaszczak"]
    };
    for (const portfolio of Object.keys(replacementCabinet)) {
        Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] =
            replacementCabinet[portfolio][0];
        Q[portfolio + "_minister"] =
            replacementCabinet[portfolio][1];
    }
    Q.family_minister_party = Q.labor_minister_party;
    Q.family_minister = Q.labor_minister;
    Q.ministry_count = 0;
    Q.cabinet_roster_government_party = "pis";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.constructive_candidate + " replaces the prime minister";
} else {
    Q.news_headline =
        "The constructive motion fails with " +
        Q.constructive_yes + " votes";
}
!}

= Constructive vote

**[+ constructive_candidate +]: [+ constructive_yes +] yes**

The nominee began from a declared camp of **[+ constructive_base +]**. Weak
relations brought **[+ constructive_relation_recruits +] partner MPs** across,
and the coalition crisis produced **[+ constructive_coalition_defections +]
more defections**. The remaining movement came from last-minute attendance and
individual decisions, not an automatic transfer of whole parties.

[? if constructive_passed: **[+ constructive_candidate +]** takes office
immediately with the MPs who signed the replacement. Lewica loses its ministries
and any of our defectors leave a permanent hole in the democratic majority; no
separate destructive vote or automatic election follows.?]
[? if not constructive_passed: The cabinet survives until the budget. Its
partners have seen exactly who was willing to leave, while PiS has learned that
this named alternative could not reach 231.?]

- @constructive_return_2026: Record the vote

@constructive_return_2026
go-to: poland_event_queue

@snap_election_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — Constitutional thresholds remain explicit, while presidential discretion, campaign choices and their political aftermaths are narrated without exposing the hidden model.
title: The constitutional route to a snap election
subtitle: Budget failure creates a choice, not an automatic dissolution
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 50
order: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and snap_election_held = 0 and snap_campaign_active = 0 and time > snap_event_deferred_time and (snap_election_requested = 1 or (budget_deadline_active = 1 and budget_deadline_time >= 0 and time >= budget_deadline_time))
on-arrival: {!
let dissolutionSupport =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0);
const oppositionToPiS = Q.government_party == "pis";
if (
    (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) >= 52 ||
    oppositionToPiS ||
    (Number(Q.ko_poll_momentum) || 0) >= 0.6
) {
    dissolutionSupport +=
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0);
}
if (
    (
        (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 0) >= 55 &&
        (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) >= 45
    ) ||
    (Number(Q.psl_poll_momentum) || 0) >= 0.7
) {
    dissolutionSupport +=
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0);
}
if (
    (
        (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0) >= 50 &&
        (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) >= 45
    ) ||
    (Number(Q.p2050_poll_momentum) || 0) >= 0.7
) {
    dissolutionSupport +=
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0);
    if ((Number(Q.centrum_relation) || 0) >= 45) {
        dissolutionSupport +=
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.centrum_seats) || 0);
    }
}
if (
    Q.government_party != "pis" &&
    (Number(Q.pis_poll_momentum) || 0) >= 0.8
) {
    dissolutionSupport +=
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0);
}
if (
    (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) >= 0.8
) {
    dissolutionSupport +=
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.konf_seats) || 0) +
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.korona_seats) || 0);
}
Q.snap_self_dissolution_support = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(460, Math.round(dissolutionSupport))
);
Q.snap_budget_deadline_ready =
    Number.isFinite(Number(Q.budget_deadline_time)) &&
    Number(Q.time) >= Number(Q.budget_deadline_time)
        ? 1
        : 0;
Q.snap_budget_petition_advocacy = 0;
Q.snap_left_can_resign_cabinet =
    Q.caretaker_government ||
    Q.government_party == "lewica" ||
    (
        Q.government_party == "independent" &&
        String(Q.government_owner || "").includes("Left-led")
    ) ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = Q.snap_election_requested
    ? "A snap-election demand reaches its constitutional route"
    : "The expired budget clock reaches the President";
!}

= Which legal trigger?

This is an **alternative path**, not historical chronology. The Sejm may
self-dissolve with 307 votes. The President may shorten the term after the
four-month budget deadline. A third failed formation attempt obliges
dissolution. A political defeat by itself does none of those things.

[? if snap_election_requested: We put the election demand on record in **[+
snap_election_request_month +]/[+ snap_election_request_year +]**. Now every
party must decide whether it will supply the votes.?][? if not
snap_election_requested: No party demand brought us here. The four-month budget
clock did.?] [? if snap_self_dissolution_support >= 307: Public declarations
now put the two-thirds majority within reach.?][? if snap_self_dissolution_support
< 307: The declared supporters still fall short of the 307 votes required to
end the term.?] [? if snap_budget_deadline_ready: The budget deadline has also
expired, leaving the Palace a separate route.?][? if not
snap_budget_deadline_ready: The budget route is not open yet.?]

- @snap_self_dissolve
- @snap_budget_deadline
- @snap_formation_ladder
- @snap_defer
- @snap_avoid
- @snap_waive_deadline

@snap_self_dissolve
title: Assemble 307 votes for Sejm self-dissolution
subtitle: Put every party's declaration to the constitutional two-thirds test.
choose-if: snap_self_dissolution_support >= 307
unavailable-subtitle: The current party-by-party count is below the constitutional two-thirds threshold.
on-arrival: snap_election_trigger = "Two-thirds Sejm self-dissolution"; position = "Snap-election campaign"; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The Sejm shortens its own term with a two-thirds vote"
go-to: snap_campaign_launch

@snap_budget_deadline
title: Petition the President after the four-month budget deadline
subtitle: The Palace decides independently whether to shorten the term.
choose-if: snap_budget_deadline_ready = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Four months have not elapsed since the recorded draft-budget submission.
on-arrival: snap_election_trigger = "Article 225 petition after the budget deadline"; snap_budget_petition_advocacy = 4; president_relation -= 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Article 225 petition reaches the President"
go-to: snap_budget_palace_decision

@snap_budget_palace_decision
title: The Palace decides under Article 225
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_budget_petition_roll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 11) - 5;
const hostileToCabinet =
    (
        Q.pres_2025_hostile_president &&
        Q.government_party != "pis"
    ) ||
    (
        Q.president_name == "Andrzej Duda" &&
        Q.government_party != "pis"
    ) ||
    (
        Q.president_name == "Rafał Trzaskowski" &&
        Q.government_party == "pis"
    );
Q.snap_budget_petition_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) * 0.30 +
    (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.25 +
    Math.max(0, 50 - (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0)) * 0.20 +
    (hostileToCabinet ? 14 : -4) +
    (Number(Q.snap_budget_petition_advocacy) || 0) +
    Q.snap_budget_petition_roll
);
Q.snap_budget_petition_approved =
    Q.snap_budget_petition_score >= 35 ? 1 : 0;
Q.news_headline = Q.snap_budget_petition_approved
    ? "The President decides to shorten the Sejm term"
    : "The President declines to shorten the Sejm term";
!}

Our petition forces a decision, not an election. The President weighs the
cabinet's disorder, the public cost of another campaign and the advantage the
Palace expects from acting now.

[? if snap_budget_petition_approved: The President signs the order shortening
the term. Parties leave the Palace for an election they can no longer defer.?]
[? if not snap_budget_petition_approved: The President refuses. The failed
budget remains the cabinet's burden, and our demand has exposed how little
control we have over the Palace.?]

- @snap_budget_approved
- @snap_budget_declined

@snap_budget_approved
title: Record the presidential shortening
view-if: snap_budget_petition_approved = 1
on-arrival: snap_election_trigger = "Presidential shortening after the budget deadline"; budget_deadline_active = 0; court_user_trust += 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The President uses Article 225 to shorten the term"
go-to: snap_campaign_launch

@snap_budget_declined
title: Record the President's refusal
view-if: snap_budget_petition_approved = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.snap_election_requested = 0;
Q.budget_deadline_active = 0;
Q.early_election_risk = Math.max(
    35,
    Q.early_election_risk - 15
);
Q.president_relation -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Article 225 window closes without an election";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

